well the apartment justice just  announced plans to appeal a San  Francisco judge's decision ordering the  continuation of the daca program a  single unelected federal judge suddenly  in charge of the entire country's  immigration policy somehow DOJ is  fighting that meanwhile though we have  new and fascinating stats tonight on  immigration both legal and illegal and  how it intersects with crime in America  as it often does  according to federal numbers released  today America's terror threat is clearly  among other things an immigration issue  of the five hundred forty nine people  convicted of terrorists between 9/11 and  the end of 2016  fully 73 percent or immigrants many men  turd this country through chain  migration and the diversity lottery both  of which allow immigrants here without  regard for their skills or how well they  would integrate into American society  and clearly many are not integrating the  DOJ estimates that more than twenty  people in this country are murdered  every year in honor killings almost  always by family members who see them as  quote too westernized about 15-hundred  are put into forced marriages in this  country annually between 2003 and 2009  immigrants to the United States  committed about 70,000 sex crimes  none of these facts require we shut down  immigration no one's arguing that but  they do demand an honest discussion not  dismissive accusations of bigotry every  time somebody raises the subject you've  heard the response a thousand times shut  up dumb American illegal aliens are more  law-abiding than you are and way more  impressive and some fake study proves  that well not so fast  a new report released by John Lott of  the Crime Prevention Research Center  takes a close look at how illegal  immigration affected crime in one state  Arizona and the numbers are stark in the  state of Arizona illegal immigrants are  more than two and a half times more  likely to commit murder as US citizens  are there almost three times as likely  to commit manslaughter far more likely  to be convicted of a sex crime against  children as well as armed robbery  convicted illegal immigrants forty-five  percent more likely to be gang members  overall young illegal immigrants break  the law and not just immigration law the  rest of the laws at twice the rate of  American citizens so for at least one  state we know that illegal immigration  is directly linked to higher crime rates  these numbers deserve honest  discussion in the halls of power not  shrieks of bigotry and angry  declarations that all immigrants our  future Medal of Honor recipients the  fact that elites don't want to have that  conversation says everything about what  the real priorities are and you're not  on the list of priorities trust Attorney  General Jeff Sessions oversaw the  release of the DOJ terrorism report and  he joins us tonight mr. Attorney General  thinks coming up you know given these  numbers it does give new urgency I think  to the immigration negotiations going on  right now in Washington you were  involved in a number of efforts I think  in oh six oh seven thirteen to scuttle  attempts at amnesty and during that time  I remember you saying the Washington  establishment supports any kind of  border enforcement as long as it doesn't  work what did you mean by that  that's exactly correct anytime a  proposal like a wall or to fix this idea  that you can claim you're afraid to go  home and you get to stay in the United  States or you have problems where we  provide subsidies to people who come  illegally the more you subsidize it the  more you get of something these kind of  failed policies are just never going to  work and the American people don't  believe in it  and we've been trying to reform it and  every time you come up with a reform  that works gets blocked and so President  Trump has said we need we have  immigration and we want immigration but  we want to vet these people we want to  know who they are and make sure they're  gonna be productive people people who  are flourished in America who are going  to not be terrorists not be criminals  and that's exactly correct for America  it's just unbelievable to me that we  have the resistance we're having today  to the reforms that are on the verge we  are close to having reforms that will  actually work today and that voters  voted for by the way in 2006 big issue  in this election Trump took it directly  to the American people it was a huge  factor in his victory yet the same crowd  that fought for the amnesty before is  still trying to scuttle good reforms  today so apparently here are features of  the proposal we're now looking at it  would fund just about 10% of the  proposed border wall about 70 miles at a  2,000 no enforcement basically you can't  deport anybody it would expand it chain  migration dreamers could bring their  relatives it makes a diversity lottery  more low-skilled it doesn't seem like  it's moving in the right direction  totally in unjustifiable that cannot be  that is not a proposal that has any  prospect of success they need to look at  the proposal at House Judiciary  Committee congressman good lad has  proposed that will work it will end the  illegality make a tremendous progress  toward ending illegality and make the  system work better that's what the  American people want and the objectors  the sanctuary cities the New Jersey  policy you just talked about those are  policies that favor illegalities they  subsidize illegality they encourage  illegality American people are sick of  that it's time to end it  the choice is clear and it's going to be  even clearer this year we're gonna have  some votes in Congress people need to be  held to account are you going to fix the  system create a system that protects  America we know that as you said  seventy-three percent of the people  who've been arrested for terrorism came  here were born abroad so if they had  been properly screened and rejected we  wouldn't have had these attacks in our  country so someone I spoke to would  direct knowledge said that in his  meeting with the President on  immigration Lindsey Graham summed up his  closing argument by reciting Emma  Lazarus's poem from the Statue of  Liberty not really a case that you'd  expect Republicans to be making why  aren't there more articulate Republican  members of the Congress making the case  that you just made well I wish there  were actually I think people need to get  focused on this we are not against  immigration the president is not against  immigration what the American people  won't have a right to and what's good  for America is a lawful system of  immigration and when we admit people to  our country we should be like Canada we  should evaluate them and make sure  they're going to be lawful they're not  threats to us they have the Education  and Skills level to prosper in America  that's good for them and good for  America what good does it do to bring in  somebody who  illiterate in their own country has no  skills and is going to struggle in our  country and not be successful that is  not what a good nation should do and we  we need to get away from it a good  debate needs to be happening this year  the president is right on the lottery  that's ridiculous how absurd is a bet  for policy for a great nation we need to  tighten up on our admission of people  from dangerous areas of the globe where  we can't vet where we have high numbers  of terrorists that live in those areas  we should certainly be more careful and  limit that kind of immigration it  strange I don't when you left this the  Senate it lost a maybe it's best voice  on it so thank you very much thank you I  appreciate it

